# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Datasets (large, and fully regenerable from the seeded generator)
#   python3 hybrid_rfi_package/dataset_generator_v3_strength.py \
#       --n_images 1000 --n_freq 276 --n_time 600 --seed 42 \
#       --output_dir "Synthetic Dataset 276x600"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Synthetic Dataset/
Synthetic Dataset 276x600/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Training run outputs.
#
# WARNING (audit): excluding these wholesale is why no reported number in this
# repository can currently be checked by a reader. The heavy binaries
# (checkpoints, TF event files, prediction dumps) are reasonable to exclude, but
# the small text artefacts that constitute the EVIDENCE for a result are not:
#
#     training_log.csv        progress.json
#     run_config.json         eval_*/metrics.json
#     eval_*/per_image_metrics.csv
#
# Those are kilobytes. Commit them (the negations below un-ignore them), or
# archive the full run directories somewhere citable (Zenodo/OSF) and link the
# DOI from the paper. See AUDIT_REPORT.md section A5.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
unet_run/
unet_run_gpu/
unet_run_faircompare/
unet_run_paperdim/
hybrid_run/
hybrid_run_paperdim/

# ...but keep the small, human-readable evidence files from any run directory.
!*/training_log.csv
!*/progress.json
!*/run_config.json
!*/eval_*/metrics.json
!*/eval_*/per_image_metrics.csv

# Results written by experiments/
!results/
results/*.npy

# Preview images (regenerable)
preview/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS -- machine-local settings do not belong in a shared repository
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Do NOT commit publisher PDFs of papers. Redistributing a paywalled article
# infringes copyright; cite the DOI instead. RFI_Using_UNET.pdf (the Elsevier
# PDF of Akeret et al. 2017) was removed for this reason -- and is still present
# in git history, which must be rewritten before the repository is made public.
# See AUDIT_REPORT.md section C1.
#
# Figures you generate yourself are fine to commit; this rule is deliberately
# narrow rather than a blanket *.pdf.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RFI_Using_UNET.pdf
